The user wants an API call for creating a Google Cloud EC2 instance with RTX A6000 GPU and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. There's confusion: Google Cloud uses Compute Engine, not EC2 (that's AWS). They want an API call. We can provide a gcloud command or REST API call. Provide example using gcloud compute instances create with machine type, GPU, image. Also mention that RTX A6000 is a GPU type: "nvidia-tesla-a6000". Provide command:

gcloud compute instances create my-instance \
  --zone us-central1-a \
  --machine-type n1-standard-8 \
  --image-family ubuntu-2004-lts \
  --image-project ubuntu-os-cloud \
  --accelerator type=nvidia-tesla-a6000,count=1 \
  --maintenance-policy TERMINATE \
  --restart-on-failure \
  --boot-disk-size 100GB \
  --boot-disk-type pd-ssd

